{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And your camp shall be holy.</b> From impurity and from abomination." "<b>And He shall see no ervat davar in you.</b> Impurity or filth or a defect in lineage, as they said, of blessed memory (Kiddushin 70b), that the Shekhinah rested only upon pedigreed families in Israel — and therefore they said that anyone registered in the archive of the kings of the House of David was of confirmed lineage without doubt (ibid. 76b)." "<b>Behind you.</b> When you turn your back to Him and pay no heed to His honor regarding any of these."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:02.667893489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}